{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "NMR", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that this sequence is most similar (38.8%) to P11. Mol Wt: 2605.162; GRAVY: -0.46; Mol Formula: C106H180N39O27S5, Mol ex coeff.: 7290. Activity: Active against Gram- E. coli D31, Pseudomonas sp.*, V. diabolicus, Vibrio MPV19 (MIC 0.012-0.096uM), Gram+ B. megaterium, and S. aureus (MIC 0.012-0.096 uM). This marine peptide has a very low MIC below 100 nM and its activity is salt-insensitive (a small effect, MIC only doubled +300 or 500 mM NaCl). In vitro Toxicity: It is not hemo.lytic or cytotoxic to mammalian cells, a promising new peptide antibiotic. Structure: You can rotate, zoom, and view the 3D structure here in the PDB. 7/2021", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "24776651", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "PLoS One. 2014 Apr 28;9(4):e95737. doi: 10.1371/journal.pone.0095737. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP03127", "source_id": "AP03127", "source_numeric_id": "03127", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP03127", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Characterization and function of the first antibiotic isolated from a vent organism: the extremophile metazoan Alvinella pompejana", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
